# The champion with the dive armed and its party budget capped (dive 3,
# divecap 16): a party of the three fastest gathered units closes on
# the nearest visible ground mover that outranges every land gun the
# army fields, drafted against the OPENING rung so it dives in time,
# with sixteen parties per match as the brake. The two brakes were
# priced from opposite ends on the same sixteen members (log
# 2026-09-13): drafting against the opening rung uncapped (dive16)
# flipped three openers at four to thirteen parties each and lost
# three champion wins to sixty-seven to ninety-three parties fed to
# the same guns; drafting against the escalating rung (dive16c) cured
# all three regressions and lost two of the three flips, the dive
# first firing at frame 226k instead of 98k-104k. Sixteen sits above
# every flip's cost and below a fifth of every regression's.
# Every other knob and every goals slot is the champion's exactly.
